Subject: [PATCH] Link the glibc compatibility shim into spirv-val

`tools/val/val.cpp` uses `std::filesystem`, which pulls libc++'s
`operations.cpp.o` into the link, and that object references an unversioned
`copy_file_range`. The hermetic toolchain's sysroot exports the symbol only as
`copy_file_range@GLIBC_2.27`, a non-default version, so the reference does not
resolve and the link fails. `//third_party/libc_compat` is the shim
`donner_cc_binary` already injects into this repository's own binaries for
exactly that reason, under the same condition; `@@//` reaches it because donner
is the root module.

diff --git a/BUILD.bazel b/BUILD.bazel
--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -316,10 +316,13 @@
     ],
     copts = COMMON_COPTS,
     visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
     deps = [
         ":spirv_tools_internal",
         ":tools_io",
         ":tools_util",
-    ],
+    ] + select({
+        "@@//build_defs:llvm_latest_linux": ["@@//third_party/libc_compat:libc_compat"],
+        "//conditions:default": [],
+    }),
 )
 
